{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children","id":1031366,"title":"Children","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-13T15:59:12-08:00","id":1031366,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Children","content":"Of the various splats which of them can have children and is there anything special about those children, I know that Dhampyrs are a thing and I'm really looking forward to half damned. Heirs to hell explained the children of demons, but what about others, can Beasts reproduce, how does it work with werewolves, let alone changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T17:24:45-08:00","id":1031389,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's any prohibitions against any of the splats having children except for vampires being dead and I think there may have been something about the Durance rendering changelings infertile. Presumably a decent number of werewolf children wind up being Wolf-Blooded, and I'd assume the child of a Beast would be a normal mortal kid but likely one touched by the Dream and thus more prone to becoming a Beast, Hero, or member of the Merrick Institute themself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T18:48:52-08:00","id":1031410,"title":"","content":"Vampires produce Dhampyrs with living humans. There is a Cr\u00f9ac rite that can render a vampire fertile, and theoretically might be adapted to produce a Vamp/Vamp offsrping, and I shudder to think what monster could result, but it is also too interesting a question not to ponder.<br /> <br /> Werewoofs produce normal humans from their couplings, but have a higher chance of produccing natural Wolf-blooded. In 1E, true-breeding wolves produce <i>Unihar</i>, which are angry spirit children that were written out in 2E because of the <i>numerous</i> fucked-up implications and secondary effects of that.<br /> <br /> Mages produce normal humans (not even more likely to be Sleepwalkers), but there are Proximi, who may result from long-term exposure of a bloodline to the Supernal, and some might claim descent from one or more Magi.<br /> <br /> Prometheans don't usually produce offspring in the traditional sense, but one book offer the possibility of Scions, human children of Prometheans who are immune to Disquiet and tend to be drawn into Promethean happenings, but aren't otherwise supernatural.<br /> <br /> Changelings...Can Changelings have children? I've not heard either way, so I'd assume they probably produce normal humans, though possibly ones attuned to the world of Faerie.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters probably produce normal human kids <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536449-homebrew-template-paragon\">(but I have Homebrew for that that I hope isn't too terrible)</a><br /> <br /> Mummies are normally infertile, but they have an Utterance that grants unnatural fertility. I don't know what would happen if they used it on themself and then had a kid, but I'd, once again, be too interested not to ponder.<br /> <br /> Demons produce Demon-Blooded, a type of Stigmatic. There are Latents (second-generation Demon-Blooded, normal humans with the potential to Stigmatize into Offspring); Offspring (1st-generation Demon-Blooded with a Glitch and an Embed); and Fractals (Demon-Blooded through both parents, since Covers are still human bodies, get one <i>or more</i> Embeds, can see through Covers, and can tell when Demons are lying intuitively). The fun thing about Demon-Bloodedness is that it can be retroactive if a Demon Pacts themself in as your parent(s).<br /> <br /> Beasts are (biologically) human, so they produce human offspring (though Beast's children are also covered in that homebrew I linked to)<br /> <br /> And we don't know about Deviants yet, and it could well vary for them from individual to individual.<br /> <br /> And then there are the literal dozens of minor templates, which I won't cover here (although special mention goes to Cambions, humans who were born as a result of dream seduction by succubus/incubus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T19:13:22-08:00","id":1031417,"title":"","content":"thanks for the info and the homebrew link<br /> what book are cambions in?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","user":"ahather","date":". 01-13-2017, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T19:14:34-08:00","id":1031418,"title":"","content":"In first edition Changelings were usually infertile, I think it's mentioned in core and I know it comes up once or twice in the splat books. Of course, Changelings are as much about exceptions as they are about rules, and at the very least there was a goblin fruit (more of a lichen really) that could make someone temporarily fertile. <br /> <br /> There were even rules for fetches having children, although it was said to be exceedingly rare, and usually not at all something you wanted to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T20:01:12-08:00","id":1031431,"title":"","content":"There's no new explicit point of infertility as far as I know in CtL 2nd, but who knows if that means it's gone or not.<br /> <br /> That'd be another cool thing to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:23:09-08:00","id":1031452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1031431#post1031431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no new explicit point of infertility as far as I know in CtL 2nd, but who knows if that means it's gone or not.<br /> <br /> That'd be another cool thing to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>In their founding myth, Spring Court comes from changeling that could not have children but very like to have and so she bargined with Spring for that. In exchange for child, she would create the Court.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:30:54-08:00","id":1031457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1031452#post1031452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In their founding myth, Spring Court comes from changeling that could not have children but very like to have and so she bargined with Spring for that. In exchange for child, she would create the Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 1st Edition, though, that was a myth. It <i>might</i> have been true. In the end, it's true in the only way that matters to changelings-in that a story is a stage for people to change on.<br /> <br /> And that quite frankly has no bearing on anything I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:38:20-08:00","id":1031461,"title":"","content":"At my own table, I had just used the rules from... I think it was Equinox Road... for Fae-Touched... I need to double check...<br /> <br /> Anyway, my ruling was that while a substantial number of Changelings were infertile with humans because of the changes wrought on them by their Durance, a fair number could still have children, BUT these children were always of special interest to the Gentry, so its an ethnically fraught decision, and most Changelings avoided having children by choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T23:58:27-08:00","id":1031482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1031461#post1031461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a fair number could still have children, BUT these children were always of special interest to the Gentry, so its an ethnically fraught decision, and most Changelings avoided having children by choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sookie Stackhouse Syndrom? ,)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T00:19:41-08:00","id":1031487,"title":"","content":"I have practical question: should supernatural offspring popup in chronicle otherwise as theoretical theme or minor template NPC? If time lapse of <i>chronicle</i> does not contain more than one year (if it's not a rape - with rape in firs chapter it's nine month) then PC can not produce offspring. Or they star as children PC (with special condition).<br /> <br /> Oh! And that's theme popup in Fables, where<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Big Bad Wolf (Bigby) and Snow White (may be they should be considered as True Fay) has seven children</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-14-2017, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T00:59:56-08:00","id":1031494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1031482#post1031482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sookie Stackhouse Syndrom? ,)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're referring to something that must have happened way after I stopped watching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:10:52-08:00","id":1031641,"title":"","content":"I just remember a text in one of the books on Changeling, I think it was the booklet Goblin Market. The guy presents at the Market his own baby, &quot;the child of a Changeling with a Fetch&quot;. Yes, the tale begins with him killing his girlfriend or spouse, I don't know, who was actually a Fetch. So Changelings are expected to not have many children, but open to a hell of a lot of strange possibilities.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12029\" data-vbnamecard=\"12029\">OsuNeko</a>, I think there are a good number of ways to explore those themes in game. If you don't want to cover a lot of time, the characters can still observe the results in the children of NPCs, learning their past stories either after or before encountering them in the present. So you put the adult, or even old, special child as an NPC, and make the backstory available. You can instead make available the records of past children of supernaturals, and those records can be the McGuffing instead of the actual children. Or, of course, you can use the PCs as the children. You'll need a far more accurate grasp of the effects you want from the beginning here, but that can open a lot of new avenues for your game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:11:33-08:00","id":1031810,"title":"","content":"I know I'd seen some references to vampires being able to pass medical inspection while under the blush of life so it could possibly be one way for children to be conceived. With a ordo dracul coil that allows the blush of life to last for 24hrs one may even be able to carry the child themself.<br /> Again, I can't say that with 100% certainly but I thought it was interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T17:09:09-08:00","id":1031889,"title":"","content":"yeah there is a sidebar in secrets of the covenants suggesting that the coil of ziva (specifically shedding the beasts skin) could be used to allow vamps to have children, and 2nd ed rules for dhampyrs (half Vampires) are coming with VtR: Half Damned, of course there's the first ed rules for them in 'night Horrors: wicked Dead'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:24:03-08:00","id":1032641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1031410#post1031410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewoofs</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I just say how much I love this typo?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:01:38-08:00","id":1032666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1032641#post1032641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say how much I love this typo?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not a typo, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:36:02-08:00","id":1033283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children#post1031366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the various splats which of them can have children and is there anything special about those children, I know that Dhampyrs are a thing and I'm really looking forward to half damned. Heirs to hell explained the children of demons, but what about others, can Beasts reproduce, how does it work with werewolves, let alone changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally they either produce humans. Which makes sense, as otherwise humanity would be extinct. On the other hand, there is literally endless field to explore if you wish, as magic of various sorts can create half/breeds and mutations of all sorts. As a mage fan, I had a concept of a chimerologist mage that playiers around with it. Good luck making the concept work on a table though, better use as NPC.<br /> So, in short there are lot of way to make whatever hybrid you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 01-17-2017, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:12:29-08:00","id":1033479,"title":"","content":"Oh, and it's quite possible that a Deviant could be the offspring of one or more supernatural beings, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:31:19-08:00","id":1033548,"title":"","content":"Vampires <i>usually</i> don't have kids, but a vampire pregnancy is covered in <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>, and we get into how that can go in the upcoming <i>Half-Damned</i>.<br /> <br /> In 2e, changelings can have children like anyone else. Strange things can happen when your mom's a changeling, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:52:29-08:00","id":1034185,"title":"","content":"I'll throw to my players the idea of a game of mortals who are each children to supernatural characters. No focus on supernatural powers of their own, just on the implications to a mortal's life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:15:48-08:00","id":1034205,"title":"","content":"<i>Chronicles of Darkness: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Runaways_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Runaways </a></i>could be pretty kickass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:17:55-08:00","id":1034207,"title":"","content":"I've run a lot of teenage games, the first Mage game I ran was ripped shamelessly from the first Runaways series.<br /> <br /> The Innocents book doesn't fit for teens at all but the 'standard' Chronicles stuff seems a bit much. I usually go with standard rules then fiddle a couple things. Size 4 is common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:56:07-08:00","id":1034358,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that video Nintendo released showing how the Switch's parental controls work is how I picture a Beast dad might hang out with his son in dad's lair.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLdWHOW9zqc\" target=\"_blank\">amazing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:43:54-08:00","id":1034667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1034207#post1034207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've run a lot of teenage games, the first Mage game I ran was ripped shamelessly from the first Runaways series.<br /> <br /> The Innocents book doesn't fit for teens at all but the 'standard' Chronicles stuff seems a bit much. I usually go with standard rules then fiddle a couple things. Size 4 is common.</div> </div> </div> </div>My 1-hour convention demo for CofD uses the standard rules for a group of high school students. I leave off Merits, though, to keep things simple. (And because it's mainly running/exploring in the woods, so a lot of common Merits wouldn't be useful.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:23:24-08:00","id":1034695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1031366-children?p=1034667#post1034667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My 1-hour convention demo for CofD uses the standard rules for a group of high school students. I leave off Merits, though, to keep things simple. (And because it's mainly running/exploring in the woods, so a lot of common Merits wouldn't be useful.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Losing, or at least limiting, Merits does make more sense for them, though, I'll keep that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:28:01-08:00","id":1036838,"title":"","content":"The ways I know of so far for making a Dampyr are Ziva coils and Primal Creation Cruac Style. <br /> <br /> Primal Creation Cruac Style can possibly lead to weirder stuff, like baby half Strix, half Void Creatures, half Cruac Gods (Cruac Gods seem similar enough to Kindred that I think they would just give birth to Dampyrs). <br /> <br /> I don't know about Changeling children, but even if they are human I could see them being born ensorcerolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}